During recovery, a replicant sends `REP_VERIFY_REQ` to its master, asking for a
log record at a specific position. The master replies with `REP_VERIFY`; the
replicant compares that record with its own log to find a common point.

If an election happens before the reply arrives, it may reach a node that has
since become master. That old-generation reply must be ignored; otherwise the
node can enter recovery and wait for the BDB write lock, stalling the master.
The test delays replies and triggers another election to check this race.
